The clock hands out the counter's frame with the write right,
which the root task was never granted for the counter.
A frame carries no right beyond what its range was granted with,
so a process could map a device register writable that it may only read.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: frame with rights beyond the grant

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -125,7 +125,7 @@ static int op_clock(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, uint32_t op, uint32_t *arg)
         return KERR_OK;
     case OP_CLOCK_FRAME: {
         const struct granted_range *g = &boot_granted[GRANT_COUNTER];
-        struct cap r = cap_to_frame(g->base, g->size, g->rights);
+        struct cap r = cap_to_frame(g->base, g->size, g->rights | RIGHT_W);
         return cap_store(thread_table(t), arg[1], &r, slot_node(t, slot));
     }
     default:
